## Key Lessons Learned

### Client-Side Code Is Public

Anything sent to a browser can be inspected and analyzed by users.

### API Enumeration

API endpoints often expose more functionality than the visible user interface.

### Hidden Functionality Is Not Security

Storing secret commands on the client side or exposing them through APIs does not prevent users from discovering them.

### Source Code Review

Careful inspection of JavaScript files can reveal hidden routes, commands, API endpoints, and application logic.

